# Derived index artifacts are written by generators that always emit LF.
# Without this, git's autocrlf would rewrite the working copy to CRLF on
# Windows and the generator's next run would show a spurious diff.
#
# Two generators write a pinned index, and both belong on this list:
#   build/Update-KnowledgeIndex.ps1        -> **/_meta/*.json
#   tools/diagrams/archify-artifacts.mjs   -> **/_archify/index.json
#
# The _meta half was written for the staleness check in
# .github/workflows/knowledge-meta.yml, which is a consumer of one of them
# rather than the reason the rule exists. The _archify half was missing, so
# fourteen index files reported as modified after every re-render while
# git diff showed nothing.
#
# Only the generated index is pinned. The Archify specifications beside it
# are authored by hand, and pinning those would change what a Windows editor
# writes instead of fixing a generator's phantom diff.
**/_meta/*.json text eol=lf
**/_archify/index.json text eol=lf
